WEBVTT

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.450
Here's breakfast.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.620
Help yourself once the medicine wears off.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.870
Medicine?

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:28.370
A bit of anesthetic. I didn't want
to risk being attacked by you again.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:36.040
Now then, I'll have you wait here
until we reach 100,000,000 views.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.870
That's the identification bracelet for dropouts.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.790
It's very convenient when recovering a corpse.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.950
Do you have any questions?

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:51.830
You'll have to speak louder than that.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:56.290
You're like a rabid dog, aren't you?

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.910
What'd you do to my damn grandpa?

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.830
I believe there's a misunderstanding.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.870
I can do many things, but controlling
life and death is not one of them.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.700
Well then, Mr. Onigasaki. Farewell.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.950
Have sweet nightmares.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:28.910
"The Ones Within"

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.870
Oh, my.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.910
Good grief. So much danger at every turn.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.450
What'd you do to Oni, you jerk?!

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.500
Mr. Onigasaki violated
another taboo last night.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.200
He invaded Floor 51 and tried to attack me.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.450
Using that sword of his,
he attempted to slit my throat.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.500
That sort of dangerous element
cannot be permitted in--

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.000
That's bullshit.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.040
You goaded him into it I bet.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.370
I did nothing at all.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:30.660
But I wonder what it was that
forced him to take such actions?

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:36.370
--Therefore, you will proceed with
the games with seven people now.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:37.950
--I won't.
--Therefore, you will proceed with
the games with seven people now.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.450
Wh-What was that, Mr. Iride?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.160
I'm on strike. Give Kaikoku back to us.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.250
I won't participate in the games till you do.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.000
Mr. Iride! Oh, Mr. Iride!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.620
How can someone like you, so faithful
to the games, say something like that?

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.870
If you refuse to participate,
you'll also get the White Room.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:07.950
That's fine. But at least let me
keep Kaikoku company.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.330
Iride...

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.120
If Akatsuki ain't playing, I ain't either.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.450
I'm not gonna do what you want.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:18.370
Me either. This is way too one-sided.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:23.250
How about this, Mr. Alpaca?
Why not postpone the games for a while?

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.000
We're all distraught by what happened to Kai.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.080
Even if you force the games to go on,
it won't produce the results you want.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.120
To be perfectly honest,
I'm rather displeased myself.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.040
What do you think about Iride?

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.950
I'm honestly suspicious of him.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.910
Oshigiri.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.120
Iride?

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.540
Would you like something to eat?

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:59.870
Himiko and the others
whipped these up for us.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:02.830
Karin made these thick mushroom pork rolls...

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.450
...and these fluorescent pink
<i>tsukudani </i>were made by Yuzu.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:11.200
And guess what? I wrapped the
seaweed around the panda rice balls.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.410
Sorry for making you guys worry.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.540
Iride...

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:21.700
Yes?

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:26.580
You're... You guys are on our side, right?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.910
Eh?

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:32.000
No, never mind... Sorry, forget I said that.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.410
I...

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:39.040
I like you, Oshigiri.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.330
I want to be on your side forever.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:46.410
Don't worry. We'll be back to eight again soon.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:52.160
Emergency notice. Everyone,
please gather on Floor 1.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:58.580
I'm offering you a chance to rescue
the dropout for a limited 72 hours.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:03.500
You are to solve the six-digit password
and open the path to the White Room.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:07.330
Without even a hint? You want us
to guess 1,000,000 times?

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:09.040
It's right here.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:16.660
Stage 8 is "White Puzzle."
The hint is one piece of these 30,000.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.950
It's on you to find this lonely piece
that doesn't fit in with its friends.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:27.450
Do you know why I chose a puzzle
this time, Ms. Roromori?

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:32.580
It's so that you understand
your place for once.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.290
Hey, what's your beef with Yuzu?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.950
It's fine, Anboy. Let's start.
We're short on time.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.160
This...

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.870
What if Sakura's still here?

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.660
In the dungeons...

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:07.200
I can't let Oshigiri see this...

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.250
This is...

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.370
There's a breeze.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.160
Is anyone there?

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:47.790
"Corners"                      "Borders"

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.910
Look. There're numbers on the back of them.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:53.870
Six digits! The same as the password, right?

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:58.040
Must mean the numbers on the
extra piece are the answer then.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.790
Hey, we really putting this together?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.750
Wouldn't it be faster
to try the 30,000 passwords?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:08.660
But if we do that, it'll be inefficient
since only one person can do it at a time.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:12.450
It's also possible we try
the right piece but input it wrong.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:16.000
There's no knowing if the puzzle
is missing pieces either.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.750
And there're so many pieces that look alike...

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.410
I wouldn't worry about that.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:23.500
Look what happens with
this corner and border piece.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.580
They stuck together!

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:29.580
The seam and numbers
on the back vanish, too.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.790
We can't put pieces together wrong.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:34.410
I guess we'll just have to build it then.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.450
That's the gist of it.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.120
However, there's no need
to complete the whole thing.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.370
Assuming it's a 200x150 piece puzzle,

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.000
the outer border including
corners is 696 pieces.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.830
"Corners: 4
Borders: 692"
the outer border including
corners is 696 pieces.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:51.700
"Corners: 4
Borders: 692"
If the pieces add up when we count them,
those can be eliminated.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:55.000
That leaves 29,305 pieces.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.080
We'll have to slim down the others bit by bit.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.790
All right, guys. Let's split
these up like I said.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:15.750
Ah, finally.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.660
It's crazy how she figured
that out in an instant.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.160
Who in the world is Yuzu anyway?

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:26.290
I only know a little from chatting with her,

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.540
but I guess she skipped grades
and finished her master's overseas.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:35.200
She does plant research at a lab
as a hobby and to earn some money,

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:38.500
but she's being scouted, too.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:42.870
The more I hear, the less I know.
How old is Yuzu anyway?

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:46.080
I'm of the belief you
shouldn't ask a girl her age.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:07.790
Without a doubt, there're people here...

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:14.040
Excuse me?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.200
Not a decent face among you.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:22.200
Who the hell are you?
You better tell us the truth!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:26.080
When asking someone for their name,
start with yours first.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.830
Huh? Who do you think you are?!

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.330
Hiro.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:32.700
"Grouchy type"

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:33.750
"Grouchy type"
"Mysterious type"

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:34.950
"Easy-to-deal-with type"
"Mysterious type"

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.290
And take off that ridiculous
mask while you're at it.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:41.040
Hiiiiro.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.660
Don't think I'm wearing this 'cuz I want to!

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.160
Oh, jeez. Good grief...

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:53.450
Sorry. He's just an idiot and
doesn't really mean any harm.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.200
I'm Nanami.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:09.000
Sorry. I don't mean any harm either.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.040
I'm here for a reason.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:24.290
And I won't leave till I'm done.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.370
I'm searching for my twin sister.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.370
Who's there?

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.120
Oshigiri?

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.870
Sakura?

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:39.580
That's right, but... Who are you?

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:41.620
Seriously?

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:43.700
What the hell are you doing?!

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:46.870
You okay, Sakura?! Don't let
your guard down around him!

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:48.500
Relax, Hiro.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:52.660
Stay back, Sakura! He'll do something
perverted if you give him a chance!

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.160
I can tell by his face!

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.250
--My, there's a weird-looking
bug stuck to my back...

00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:00.120
--My spine! My spine!
--My, there's a weird-looking
bug stuck to my back...

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:03.870
Oh, you're awake? Sorry about earlier.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:07.410
I had to know if you're friend or foe
before it got out of hand.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:11.750
And, well, I gave you a physical exam.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.450
Nanami! Don't incite the hooligan!

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:18.500
But the fact you're wearing that means...

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.910
Who are you guys anyway?

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.660
Right, right. Self-introductions.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.000
I'm Nanami Omejima.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.200
That kid is Chihiro Akafuda.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:32.000
The flower among us is Sakura Oshigiri.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.620
Allow me to welcome you
to the underground, comrade.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:45.950
U-Um, I've never done
a jigsaw puzzle before...

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.790
How long does it usually take to finish?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:53.700
It depends on the person, but it took me
half a day to do a 1,000-piece puzzle.

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.160
Half a day?

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.910
So 15 days for 30,000 pieces.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.450
With seven people, that's over two days.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:03.080
W-We can pull it off then.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:06.450
But that only applies to a normal puzzle.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:11.540
Since these white pieces don't give
any hints, it'll take many times longer.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:16.500
We'll be fine, meow!
Puzzles are my specialty!

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.080
Thirty thousand pieces will be a cinch.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:23.830
But I'll need all your help to do it,
so enough of the chitchat.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.000
Let's all get back to work!

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:27.620
Y-You're right.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.660
Let's do our best!

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:42.120
Here, hopefully this size fits you.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.500
Sorry about this.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:46.790
It's okay. All this is stolen anyway.

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:51.290
Why not change while you're at it?
A kimono with sneakers seems weird.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:55.910
Kids these days are truly frightening!

00:13:55.910 --> 00:14:00.080
They undress and change
clothes in front of a lady!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:03.700
Oh, please. Aren't you a gentleman?

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.910
Anyway, it's such a surprise.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:09.660
That Sakura's brother came here, that is.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.250
For now, let's exchange information.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:17.910
Only the three of us are in
the underground at the moment.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:22.250
I'm from 9th Avenue, so I've
been here around four years now.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.290
Hiro and Sakura are both 11th Avenue--

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:29.000
Hold up. What do you mean
by 9th and 11th Avenue?

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.500
You mean there're other places like this?

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.830
Oh, you don't even know that.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.540
When we say 13th Avenue,
it's not some unique place.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:41.620
9th Avenue and 11th Avenue
were also the same place.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:45.700
Every time the members change,
the city name is updated.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:48.910
We're on an uninhabited
island far off in the sea.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:52.410
Occasionally, people come
and go to restock supplies,

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:55.870
but that alpaca makes sure
they're hidden from sight.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:58.830
I knew other people had to be involved...

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:05.250
Yeah... There's even helicopters that
fly in while you're busy playing games.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:10.160
Ironic, isn't it? The dropouts are
the ones who can see the big picture.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.450
Nanami! Big trouble, Nanami!

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:15.200
Sakura... Sakura's missing!

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:26.910
Hey!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.200
Go and sleep, would you?

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:33.580
S-Sorry! I'm fine!
What should I work on next?!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.790
Hey!

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.450
I-I'm fine!

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:43.200
Go and sleep for crying out loud!

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.290
B-But...!

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:48.540
Shuddap! If you're tired and screw up,
you'll only be dragging us down!

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:52.620
Let me translate. "I'm worried
about you, so I want you to sleep."

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:55.500
"And sweet dreams," he says.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.290
There's a nap room right next door.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:02.080
I'm so sorry...

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:04.450
Good grief.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:08.580
Aikawa, you're really pushing
yourself. Aren't you sleepy?

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.580
We have to get... Kaikoku back.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.950
A-Aikawa...

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.410
Hey, Missy.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:27.330
Hey, Mister. Did you get a makeover?

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.450
No, not quite.

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:33.370
You shouldn't be roaming alone
without even leaving a note.

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:35.870
It's fine, I always do it.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:38.750
Nanami and Hiro are a bit overprotective.

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:46.040
Hold it. Get back here, Oshigiri girl.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:47.660
It's Sakura.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:52.620
Sakura. This isn't the way back, you know.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:56.620
There're radio parts that might
still be usable up this way.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:17:02.000
One of my tools broke the last time I came,
but this time I'll bring it all back.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.250
My brother...

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:13.370
Is Zakuro... all right?

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:17.830
Who knows?

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:22.790
But the last time I saw him, he was
stuffing his face with mushroom pasta.

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:24.870
That seems all right to me.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.250
He never changes.

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:34.290
You up? You collapsed about
an hour after Inaba napped.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.830
Remember that?

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:40.750
Swap with me since you're
awake. I'm taking a nap.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.790
Hey, what was that about earlier?

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.330
Meaning what?

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:54.200
In the lounge. You said something
weird to Akatsuki, right?

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:58.660
Yuzu was acting strange, too.
Do you know something?

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:04.040
Quit doubting people in secret.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.250
You're awful good at that.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:12.790
I just copy Nanami.
He's pretty amazing though.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.500
He makes radios and
stun guns like it's nothing.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:18.830
Oh? That was his creation?

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:22.370
Before, he was hoping
to get these parts, so...

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.620
I-I'm giving it to him as a present.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:32.370
Poor Hiro. When we get back,
I'll be nicer to him.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:37.410
By the way, I guess there're mermaids here.

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:38.450
Mermaids?

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.790
Nanami said him and a friend
saw one long ago.

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:44.500
It had long hair like a ghost.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.250
A ghost?

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:49.950
Yup! Like a mermaid and ghost all in one!

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:55.950
Wish I could see one! I wonder how
it walks and breathes. If I had to guess...

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:57.410
Huh? What's wrong?

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:00.790
No, something touched my leg...

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:01.660
Mister!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.040
Stay back!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:16.500
Impossible...

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:17.330
"Impossible"
Impossible...

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:24.410
"Impossible"
Impossible! Impossible! Impossible!
Impossible! Impossible! Impossible!

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.620
Puzzles are my forte, so I know.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:30.410
I've built thousands and thousands
like this since I was young.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:35.950
That's why I can say for sure.
We'll never make it in time.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.750
Yuzu?

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.040
Are you all right?

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:49.910
I'm fine.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:52.250
But, there's blood on your nail.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:56.620
Oh, it's just one of my habits.
Doing this helps me concentrate.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:59.830
You're such a worry-wort, Karirin!

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:02.950
Yuzu.

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:11.620
If we finish, I'll do any
one thing that you want.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:14.870
So please don't give up just yet.

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:24.290
That's right...

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:04.290
If only I knew the numbers
on those first two pieces!

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:08.910
It was 001453 and 017491.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.080
Are you serious?

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.790
What's the point of me lying?

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:21.540
I'm sure of it. I never forget
things I hear or see.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:23.870
Who knew Karin had such a setting?

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:28.330
Don't call it a setting. And I told you
in the forest we met in, remember?

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:30.410
Oh, really?

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.290
Is that what this is?

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:36.750
I see the way...

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:41.660
Everyone, please...

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.950
I need your help.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.000
All right, we've got this!

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.750
Let's finish this and
smack the hell out of Kai!

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:59.120
Yeah!

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:09.410
Is this... a mermaid?
